# Clean code and structure (backend)

- Keep changes focused; do not refactor unrelated modules.
- Prefer small, composable units: one concern per file where practical.
- Remove dead code; avoid duplicated validation or auth logic — extract shared middleware or helpers.
- Favor explicit error handling: map known failures to **`ApiError`** and let the **central `errorHandler`** serialize JSON.
- **Intended layout** (evolve as needed):
  - **`src/index.ts`** — process entry (listen); loads config via imports.
  - **`src/app.ts`** — Express factory: global middleware (helmet, cors, json), mount routers, **404**, **error handler** (in that order).
  - **`src/routes/`** — Top-level routers (`health`, **`routes/v1/index.ts`** for versioned APIs).
  - **`src/modules/<domain>/`** — Feature slices that will grow together:
    - **`<name>.routes.ts`** — `Router` + middleware chain only.
    - **`<name>.controller.ts`** — thin handlers; call **`parseBody`/validators** or read **`res.locals`**; no Prisma.
    - **`<name>.middleware.ts`** — request-scoped checks (e.g. body parse → `res.locals`).
    - **`<name>.schemas.ts`** — Zod schemas (HTTP boundary).
    - **`user.service.ts`** (or `<domain>.service.ts`) — use-cases; orchestrate repositories; map persistence errors to **`ApiError`** where appropriate.
    - **`user.repository.ts`** — Prisma only; no HTTP types.
  - **`src/middleware/`** — Cross-cutting Express middleware (`errorHandler`, `notFoundHandler`, shared auth/OTP stubs).
  - **`src/lib/`** — Shared utilities (`asyncHandler`, `ApiError`, `prisma`, `validateRequest`, Prisma error helpers).
  - **`src/config/`** — Validated env (prefer **Zod** + fail-fast on boot).
  - **`src/types/`** — Shared string unions / DTOs that mirror Prisma when tooling is flaky.
  - **`prisma/`** — `schema.prisma` and migrations.
  - **`Backend/docs/features/`** — feature specs for this workspace; cross-client contracts in repo **`docs/authentication/`** when applicable.
- Every implemented behavior should map to a documented acceptance criterion in the relevant feature doc.
